herence": 0.65, "environmental_progression": 0.45, "target_achievement": 0.38, "overall_confidence": 0.48, "feedback": "The route is connected and conserves atoms with the supplied coefficients. Its principal bottlenecks are rxn_005 and rxn_006: supplying reducing equivalents fixes their equations but does not establish selective deoxygenation or reductive cyanation. Competing thione reduction/desulfurization and cyanide/sulfide inhibition of candidate hydrogenation catalysts remain unresolved. The final hydrolyses could produce an L-containing racemate if prolinonitrile were obtained, but their required acidity, temperature and residence time are unspecified.", "approved": false, "problematic_reactions": ["rxn_001", "rxn_004", "rxn_005", "rxn_006", "rxn_013", "rxn_014"], "suggestions": ["Establish rxn_005 and rxn_006 experimentally on the named substrates, including competing products and sulfur fate.", "Specify photochemical conditions, a geochemically realistic hydrogenation catalyst, and transfer procedures addressing catalyst passivation and intermediate loss.", "Measure acrolein monoaddition selectivity, thiolactam formation and both hydrolysis rates under the proposed conditions."]}, {"pathway_id": "P2", "reaction_scores": {"rxn_002": 0.55, "rxn_003": 0.84, "rxn_004": 0.65, "rxn_005": 0.32, "rxn_006": 0.25, "rxn_013": 0.81, "rxn_014": 0.84}, "chemical_feasibility": 0.47, "pathway_coherence": 0.63, "environmental_progression": 0.43, "target_achievement": 0.35, "overall_confidence": 0.45, "feedback": "Accepting propanedial as an explicit boundary input, rxn_002 is formally reasonable but lacks evidence for selective monoamination rather than carbonyl reduction, further amination or condensation. Reactive aminoaldehyde delivery to the surface stage is also unspecified. The downstream deoxygenation and reductive cyanation remain the dominant unresolved transformations. All equations are balanceable; these concerns concern selectivity, kinetics and environmental i