nation while retaining the nitrile.", "Identify conditions for rxn_009 that favor cyclic-imine formation over complete hydrogenation, and quantify the product distribution.", "Show that pyrroline survives transfer to cyanation conditions and establish subsequent nitrile and amide hydrolysis rates."]}, {"pathway_id": "P6", "reaction_scores": {"rxn_002": 0.55, "rxn_003": 0.84, "rxn_007": 0.35, "rxn_009": 0.48, "rxn_012": 0.87, "rxn_013": 0.81, "rxn_014": 0.84}, "chemical_feasibility": 0.57, "pathway_coherence": 0.73, "environmental_progression": 0.46, "target_achievement": 0.45, "overall_confidence": 0.54, "feedback": "The cyclic-imine cyanation and hydrolysis segment is chemically credible. Upstream, selective propanedial monoamination, cyanohydrin deoxygenation and partial nitrile hydrogenation are not demonstrated under specified conditions. In particular, H2 availability alone does not establish selective production and preservation of pyrroline. The graph reaches racemic proline formally, but actual production depends on resolving these upstream selectivity and transfer problems.", "approved": false, "problematic_reactions": ["rxn_002", "rxn_007", "rxn_009", "rxn_013", "rxn_014"], "suggestions": ["Measure monoamination selectivity and reactive intermediate lifetimes starting from the stated propanedial input.", "Validate rxn_007 and selective imine production in rxn_009 with explicit catalysts and product balances.", "Specify conditions that preserve pyrroline during transfer and complete both hydrolysis stages."]}, {"pathway_id": "P7", "reaction_scores": {"rxn_010": 0.6, "rxn_011": 0.91, "rxn_012": 0.87, "rxn_013": 0.81, "rxn_014": 0.84}, "chemical_feasibility": 0.76, "pathway_coherence": 0.87, "environmental_progression": 0.57, "target_achievement": 0.69, "overall_confidence": 0.71, "feedback": "This is a credible conditional route: 4-aminobutanal cyclization, cyclic-imine cyanation and aminonitrile hydrolysis are sound transformations. The main bottleneck is s